            <ArticleTitle>Chronic total occlusion of the left main coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>94-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e32801105df</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Total chronic occlusion of the left main coronary artery is a rare angiographic finding in a catheterization laboratory and its treatment rarely is reported. We describe a patient with angiographic findings of chronic total occlusion of the left main coronary artery with left coronary circulation collateralized from the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
